0,Kalaamaya language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalaamaya_language,"Kalaamaya, also spelled Karlamay, is a Pama-Nyungan language of Western Australia. It is poorly attested, but appears to be a close relative of Noongar. [4] A variety called Nyaki Nyaki (Njakinjaki) has been variously said to be a dialect of Nyungar or of Kalaamaya. [5] Natingero has also been listed as a dialect, but it is only 40% lexically similar. As of 2015, a single fluent speaker ...",Kalaamaya,Australian
1,Kalamaia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalamaia,Kalamaia The Kalamaia are an Aboriginal Australian people of the Wheatbelt and Goldfields-Esperance regions of Western Australia.,Kalaamaya,Australian
2,Kalaamaya language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/kalaamaya_language,"Kalaamaya is a member of the Pama-Nyungan language family, which encompasses the majority of Australian Aboriginal languages and is characterized by shared phonological and grammatical features across its branches.",Kalaamaya,Australian
